#!/bin/sh
# Project-specific pre-push guards — a MENU OF SHAPES to copy FROM.
#
# APPEND what you need to .githooks/pre-push-project, AFTER its BLUEPRINT:END
# marker. Do NOT copy this file over it: `pre-push-project` ships already
# populated, wiring the regression suites that guard the blueprint-managed
# machinery your project runs (blueprint pull/drift/a2bp, signal-set.sh, the
# feed, the hooks, the gate renderer). Overwriting it takes all of them off your
# push path in one command, and the gate keeps printing PASSED over the
# remainder — which is BUG-004 and A-22 exactly, so it would not look like a
# mistake (BUG-028).
#
# The MARKERS are what split ownership (BUG-029). Between BLUEPRINT:BEGIN and
# BLUEPRINT:END the blueprint owns the file and `blueprint pull` replaces the
# region — that is how a suite added upstream arrives with something to invoke
# it. After BLUEPRINT:END the project owns it and pull preserves it
# byte-for-byte. The file used to be excluded from sync wholesale, which kept
# your guards safe and left every derived gate frozen at its bootstrap commit.
#
# Editing INSIDE the region loses the edit at the next pull. If the change is
# generic, send it up instead: `blueprint a2bp .githooks/pre-push-project`.
#
# Examples (uncomment and adapt):

